      "message": "Say what is true about importing, the door and joining\n\nImporting is the operator's, as the operating document said and the\ncode did not: an import is the forge's own machine fetching from an\naddress of the caller's choosing, which is not an owner's to make it\ndo however much the repository is theirs. The check now asks for the\nunscoped admin, the New page shows the import field only to somebody\nit would not refuse, and the walk that proves a local source is the\noperator's proves an https one is too.\n\nThe door's path list gains the web twins of what it already refused\n— the reports page, a repository's mirror form — and the binding of\na workload identity, so the public listener answers those in the\nsame shape as the rest. The sign-up form no longer confirms which\nnames exist: taken or reserved, the answer is the same.\n\nAnd three sentences that had gone false: the README no longer says\na way to join without an invitation is missing (--open-signup is\nthat); the agents document says an owner registers agents too; and\n\"What is yours\" says how an owner leaves with everything at once —\nby asking, since the export runs on the box — rather than that no\nexport exists.\n\nChange-Id: Idocs0114\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
